                <pb facs="0236" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 154.</note>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[By cable telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Bancroft to Mr. Davis.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 14, 1870</date>. (Received August
                    15.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Prussia opens credit for Washburne. * * * * German army prepared to turn French
                    army north and south to save themselves: French abandons Moselle line. Next
                    defensible line the Marne.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BANCROFT.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
